    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I expect `return value` to be a comfortably rare command to appear in a `prange` loop, so this is unlikely to pose a problem for the average user. But this bug silently changes the return value and that's prone to remain undetected in many cases _if_ it is used.\n\nThe assumption that it's rarely used might make it possible for us to fix this even in a 3.2.x point release. Although at the same time, it gives us little reason to risk a disruption for it. It's probably been broken forever.",
